iption":"historic region and former province of Libya","inception":null,"dissolved":null,"enwiki":"Tripolitania","summary":"Tripolitania  (Arabic: طرابلس), historically known as the Tripoli region, is a historic region and former province of Libya.\nThe region had been settled since antiquity, first coming to prominence as part of the Carthaginian empire. Following the defeat of Carthage in the Punic Wars, Ancient Rome organized the region (along with what is now modern day Tunisia and eastern Algeria), into a province known as Africa, and placed it under the administration of a proconsul. During the Diocletian reforms of the late 3rd century, all of North Africa was placed into the newly created Diocese of Africa, of which Tripolitania was a constituent province."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q192435","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q3579","value_label":"Tripoli","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Tripoli"},{"qid":"Q192435","kind":"government","value_qid":"Q4096586","value_label":"British Military Administration","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P122","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"British Military Administration"}],"people":{},"media":{},"names":["Regio Tripolitana","Tarabulus","Trablusgarp Bölgesi","Tripolitaine","Tripolitana","Tripolitania","Tripolitanie","Tripolitanien","Tripolitanië","Tripolitânia","Trypolitania","Ţarābulus","Τριπολίτιδα","Триполитана","Триполитания","Триполитида","إقليم طرابلس","تريبولتانا","تريبوليتانيا","تریپولیتانیا","طرابلس","ولاية طرابلس","ولاية طرابلس الغرب","त्रिपोलितानिया","Ṭarābulus","Ṭrables","トリポリタニア","トリポリタニア共和国","泰拉布魯斯","泰拉布鲁斯","的黎波里塔尼亚"]}